-- title:
--   Residual eigensystem of g occurs in the Tate-module Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and a prime $p$. Assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeInputsAll N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeInputsAll.html#L8), i.e. for every prime $\ell$ the package `HeckeInputsAlong` holds over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for level $N$ and $\ell$ (integrality of the two Hecke correspondences $\alpha,\beta$ at level $N\ell$, existence of principal divisors for the base-changed function field, finiteness along $\alpha$, together with the fundamental identity for $\beta$ and the norm formula for $\alpha$), and assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L25), i.e. the endomorphisms `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ` of $J_0(N)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base-changed modular function field commute pairwise. Let $g$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$ which is a normalised eigenform in the sense that its $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1=1$, multiplicativity at coprime indices, and the usual two-term and three-term recursions at powers of primes dividing, resp. not dividing, $N$. Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ and $\varphi\colon\overline{\mathbb Z}\to k$ a ring homomorphism from the integral closure of $\mathbb Z$ in $\mathbb C$. Give $J_0(N)$ the $\mathbb T=\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,\mathrm{Nat.Primes}\,\mathbb Z$-module structure `heckeModuleBar N`, under which $X_\ell$ acts by `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ`, and let $\mathcal A\subseteq \mathrm{End}_{\mathbb Z_p}(T_pJ_0(N))$ be the $\mathbb Z_p$-subalgebra generated by the image of the induced ring homomorphism `tateHeckeRep p (JZero N)`, where $T_pJ_0(N)$ is the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in $J_0(N)$ with $p^nx_n=0$ and $px_{n+1}=x_n$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\psi\colon\mathcal A\to k$ such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ there exists an algebraic integer $a\in\overline{\mathbb Z}$ with $a=a_\ell(g)$ in $\mathbb C$ and $\psi$ of the image of $X_\ell$ equal to $\varphi(a)$. Only the values at the $T_\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$ are pinned down; nothing is asserted about the operators at primes dividing $N$ or at $p$.
--
--   This says that the eigensystem of $g$ reduced through $\varphi$ occurs as a character of the $p$-adic Hecke algebra acting on the Tate module of $J_0(N)$, equivalently that the associated maximal ideal lies in the support of $T_pJ_0(N)$. It feeds the construction of a Hecke character valued in a discrete valuation ring, and thence the mod-$p$ Galois representation attached to $g$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_IsNormalizedEigenform_exists_ringHom_adjoin_tateHeckeRep_jZero_eq_residual.lean

